# Layer 4 working memory: per-agent dossiers and claim boards.
#
# The directory contents are ignored, NOT the directory itself. Git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so `.agents/` as the rule would make the
# negations below impossible to express.
#
# Two research documents are committed as deliberate exceptions. They are the
# evidence behind the severity floors in BCH-004 and the model-pool choices in
# BCH-007, they took real work, and they existed on one disk with no backup.
# The worklogs stay out: they are scratch, and they churn every session.
.agents/*
!.agents/bench-taxonomy-research.md
!.agents/bench-model-survey.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*

# Run artifacts (provenance lives in docs/study/, not in git blobs)
runs/
*.sqlite
*.db

# Catch-up reviews. Written for the owner to read once, not repo documents.
docs/study/REVIEW-*.md

# Unattended run logs. Appended to by scripts/overnight.cmd.
logs/
